pioarduino (6.2.0-1~ppa2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Rebuild from the pioarduino repository rather than by hand. The
    6.2.0-1~ppa1 debs in the registry were built in October 2026 from a
    packaging tree that no longer exists; this revision is the first one
    that any checkout can reproduce. The source is the same PyPI sdist,
    pinned by sha256 in debian/upstream/sdist.sha256.
  * d/p/relax-deps.patch widens two pip pins, unchanged in substance from
    the October build: bottle "== 0.13.*" becomes ">= 0.12" for noble,
    which ships 0.12.25; and starlette "< 1" becomes "< 2", since
    stonking ships 1.7.0 and the fork's starlette-facing code is identical
    to upstream platformio 6.2.0, which declares "< 2" itself.
  * Stays on 6.2.0 rather than taking 6.2.0.post1: that release raises the
    starlette floor to ">=1.3.1", which noble (0.31.1) and resolute
    (0.50.0) cannot meet, so taking it would mean dropping two of the
    three series or forcing a floor upstream raised deliberately.

 -- Robert August Vincent II (Bob) <pillarsdotnet@gmail.com>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 10:00:00 -0500

pioarduino (6.2.0-1~ppa1~ubuntu26.04.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging of upstream release 6.2.0, from the PyPI sdist, for
    ppa:pillarsdotnet/ppa and the Forgejo registry.
  * Conflicts with platformio: the fork ships the same module, the same
    entry points and the same udev rule.
  * The fork's extra dependencies -- certifi, intelhex and rich-click --
    are in Ubuntu for all three series.

 -- Robert August Vincent II (Bob) <pillarsdotnet@gmail.com>  Sat, 18 Oct 2026 08:00:00 -0400
